  "title": "Lead, Pull and Shut: duc, tract and clud",
  "short": "duc means lead, tract means pull and clud and clus mean shut.",
  "trouble": "tract (pull) also names a stretch of land or a pamphlet; the root idea is \"drawn out.\"",
  "prereqs": [
    "roots.ced-gress"
  ],
  "xp": 1,
  "viz": [
    "vo-roots",
    "vo-word"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "To <i>conduct</i> an orchestra is to lead it, and to <i>produce</i> is to lead something forth. <b>duc</b> (also <b>duct</b>) means “lead.” A <i>tractor</i> pulls, and to <i>attract</i> is to pull toward: <b>tract</b> means “pull” or “draw.” And to <i>include</i> is to shut in, to <i>exclude</i> to shut out: <b>clud</b> (also <b>clus</b>) means “shut.”"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-scene",
        "opts": {
          "scene": {
            "bg": "park",
            "cast": [
              {
                "who": "pip",
                "x": 36,
                "pose": "pull",
                "mood": "determined",
                "face": "left"
              }
            ],
            "props": [
              {
                "kind": "wagon",
                "x": 66,
                "s": 1.7
              },
              {
                "kind": "teddy",
                "x": 66,
                "y": 12,
                "s": 1.3
              }
            ],
            "labels": [
              {
                "text": "TRACT = PULL",
                "x": 50,
                "y": 92
              }
            ],
            "alt": "A boy pulls a wagon with a teddy bear riding in it."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A boy pulls a wagon with a teddy bear riding in it."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>duc</b>, <b>duct</b> = <b>lead</b>. <b>tract</b> = <b>pull, draw</b>. <b>clud</b>, <b>clus</b> = <b>shut, close</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "duc",
            "tract",
            "clud"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on duc, tract and clud."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>deduce</b><br>to reach a conclusion by reasoning",
            "de- <i>from</i> + <b>duc</b> <i>lead</i> + -e<br>→ “lead from (the evidence)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>educate</i></b><br>to teach",
            "e- <i>out</i> + <b>duc</b> <i>lead</i> + -ate<br>→ “lead out”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>intractable</b><br>hard to manage, control or solve",
            "in- <i>not</i> + <b>tract</b> <i>handle, pull</i> + -able <i>able to be</i><br>→ “not able to be handled”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>protracted</b><br>lasting longer than expected or usual",
            "pro- <i>forward</i> + <b>tract</b> <i>draw</i> + -ed<br>→ “drawn out”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>attract</i></b><br>to draw something closer",
            "at- <i>toward</i> + <b>tract</b> <i>pull</i><br>→ “pull toward”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>distract</i></b><br>to draw attention away",
            "dis- <i>away</i> + <b>tract</b> <i>pull</i><br>→ “pull away”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>preclude</b><br>to make impossible in advance",
            "pre- <i>before</i> + <b>clud</b> <i>shut</i> + -e<br>→ “shut off before”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>conclusive</b><br>settling a question beyond doubt",
            "con- <i>completely</i> + <b>clus</b> <i>shut</i> + -ive<br>→ “shutting (the question) completely”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>reclusive</b><br>avoiding the company of others",
            "re- <i>away</i> + <b>clus</b> <i>shut</i> + -ive<br>→ “shut away”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "The <b>protracted</b> meeting ran two hours past its end time. What does <i>protracted</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>pro-</b> (forward) + <b>tract</b> (draw, pull) + <b>-ed</b>.",
          "Literally: “drawn forward,” drawn out like a long piece of taffy.",
          "The sentence fits: the meeting dragged on."
        ],
        "a": "Lasting longer than expected or usual."
      },
