      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "The word <i>tract</i> by itself has other meanings: a stretch of land, or a short pamphlet. Both come from the same Latin root, but neither means “pull” today. Use the root inside longer words: <i>intractable</i>, <i>protracted</i>, <i>attract</i>."
      },
      {
        "t": "note",
        "html": "Detectives <b>deduce</b>: they lead (<i>duc</i>) a conclusion out from (<i>de-</i>) the clues. When the evidence is <b>conclusive</b>, it shuts (<i>clus</i>) the case completely."
